                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6639: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-10T15:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1934—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>149. Your 241, May 3, 3 p.m. Upon receipt of invitation or of notice of
                    convocation Department desires that you instruct Mayer to attend meetings of the
                    China Technical Committee in the same capacity as that of the previous American
                    representatives, namely, informally and as an unofficial observer. If, however,
                    you have any reason to believe that the Committee will, or if after convening
                    the Committee proceeds to, take formal notice of Japanese allegations with
                    regard to political activities of the Committee, you should report to the
                    Department by telegraph and Mayer should refrain from attending meetings of the
                    Committee until he is again authorized specifically to do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
